questions.stem:
Consider the following code segment.

```text
IF (age < 17)
{
   price ← 5
}
ELSE
{
   IF (member)
   {
      price ← 8
   }
   ELSE
   {
      IF (age ≥ 52)
      {
         price ← 7
      }
      ELSE
      {
         price ← 12
      }
   }
}
DISPLAY (price)
```

What is displayed when age is 14 and member is false?

Consider the following procedure.

```text
PROCEDURE find(list, limit)
{
   FOR EACH item IN list
   {
      IF (item > limit)
      {
         RETURN (item)
      }
   }
   RETURN (-1)
}
```

What is returned by `find([19, 6, 12, 27, 8, 23], 19)`?

The following code segment is intended to display the number of elements in `nums` that are greater than 7.

```text
count ← 0
FOR EACH n IN nums
{
   IF (n ≥ 7)
   {
      count ← count + 1
   }
}
DISPLAY (count)
```

When `nums` is `[24, 22, 10, 7, 25]`, the code displays 5 instead of 4. Which change corrects the error?

